A||||1||Spektrum-87GT||rebuilding the 3.4 dohc... a hard job?||||1||
Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||09-29-2001||09:41 PM||||i'm looking into getting a 3.4 dohc engine with 40k miles... one of the valve seats has pulled out... i've got two questions... does that require a rebuild? and if it does... i've heard the 3.4 dohc is a real pain to rebuild because of the way the camshafts are set up.. all info on the subject would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||09-29-2001||11:10 PM||||Actually, it's pretty normal. With only 40k, just have both heads done and bolt them on. At the same time, it seems odd that this happened at 40k miles.<P>Setting the cams is actually easier than it sounds, but you will need to fabricate the cam hold-down tool and cam turning tool.<BR>I can scan the pics if you need them. They are reasonable easy to make. <P>What you do it lock the cams, release the lock bolts and turn the crank to pick up each cam as you rotate it. After I'd done it once, I could do it in 5 minutes max. It's easier to do out of the car though.<P>||||reg||1
